00:04:48.939 --> 00:04:52.139
I've switched this to a subsurface.

127
00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:53.379
In that subsurface,

128
00:04:53.379 --> 00:04:56.939
I went in here and created a series of network nodes

129
00:04:56.939 --> 00:04:59.220
that allow me to have precise control.

130
00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.819
One of them, I have noise control where I have lerp.

131
00:05:01.819 --> 00:05:02.879
And what happens with the lerp,

132
00:05:02.879 --> 00:05:05.420
it takes 50-50 between these two guys

133
00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:07.379
and combines them in such a way

134
00:05:07.379 --> 00:05:08.779
so that I can have an alpha

135
00:05:08.779 --> 00:05:11.180
if I wanted to via a texture

136
00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:14.399
or if I wanted to do it via a constant

137
00:05:14.399 --> 00:05:19.649
or I wanted to have it as a scalar parameter.

138
00:05:19.949 --> 00:05:22.750
Here, we have the amount of noise coming through.

139
00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.709
We have a multiply and we take that to a lerp.

140
00:05:25.709 --> 00:05:26.670
And then we just kind of,

141
00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.990
I just layer the noise in such a way.

142
00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:31.990
So there's noise stacking on top of noise.

143
00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.180
And then we have control.

144
00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:35.019
Now, if I wanted to,

145
00:05:35.019 --> 00:05:37.660
I could do an overall control of all of these

146
00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.620
and put another either lerp or multiply

147
00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.120
with a scalar parameter

148
00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:46.420
to be able to take care of that if I needed.

149
00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.660
Now, if we go down low,

150
00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.360
let's go and take a look here.

151
00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:54.600
We have an opacity control using Fresnel Index in here.

152
00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.279
So we're using that Fresnel Index to control this.

153
00:05:57.279 --> 00:06:01.000
And this allows me to have a bit more finite

154
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:01.920
look and feel.

155
00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:02.759
If we go in here,

156
00:06:02.759 --> 00:06:05.800
let's go down to those areas or up in this case.

157
00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.240
And you'll see we have a Fresnel Index here.

158
00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.959
And like I showed you before,

159
00:06:09.959 --> 00:06:13.160
we can make it so that the light is passing through more

160
00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:16.959
or is a little more solid looking in our look and feel.

161
00:06:16.959 --> 00:06:19.600
And you'll see there's also subsurface amount.

162
00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:22.120
How much of that subsurface look do we want?

163
00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:25.000
And as we lower this actually looks pretty cool.

164
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.220
And it looks like a really,

