00:07:52.779 --> 00:07:54.579
and you can see it subtly change,

200
00:07:54.579 --> 00:07:57.699
but it mainly hits right around these lower numbers

201
00:07:57.699 --> 00:08:00.500
where we can mess with that Fresnel Index control.

202
00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.759
And again, remember, if you remember

203
00:08:01.759 --> 00:08:03.379
from the foundation classes,

204
00:08:03.379 --> 00:08:06.540
your Fresnel Index is based on where your angle is

205
00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.579
on this object in the scene

206
00:08:08.579 --> 00:08:10.639
and how that light, it tries to imitate that.

207
00:08:10.639 --> 00:08:13.019
Like if you're looking at a pole from different angles,

208
00:08:13.019 --> 00:08:15.180
that's pretty much what that's trying to do

209
00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:18.279
is imitate that how that refraction occurs.

210
00:08:18.279 --> 00:08:22.959
So if we go down here to a spec reflect thickness,

211
00:08:22.959 --> 00:08:25.139
